# Keep LF on every checkout, including Windows.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites tracked text
# files to CRLF when it checks them out. lab/entrypoint.sh is bind-mounted into
# the app container and run as its entrypoint, so a CR at the end of the shebang
# line stops the container from starting. These rules override the local setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.mo binary

# Exempt from the LF rule above.
#
# E-mail fixtures are wire format. RFC 5322 puts CRLF at the end of every
# header line, and the ticket-from-e-mail tests parse these bytes as they
# stand, so normalising them breaks the test suite.
*.eml -text

# Vendored asset. It ships as its author released it.
src/helpdesk/static/helpdesk/jquery.translate-debug-all.js -text
